	"description": [
		"Students consider how norms of masculinity and femininity are expressed through music in historical and contemporary contexts around the world. Through investigating relationships between music, gender, and sexuality from a variety of analytical perspectives structured around ethnographic case studies, students encounter multiple models of music research, which they use to guide their own ethnographic projects. Prerequisite: MUSIC 141 or permission of instructor."
